Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:16:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 324/333] Assembly: a part put in goes beside the others, not
 on top of them

"Put Part" put every part at the origin (each time the panel opened, the
first one without an offset; the next ones 15% of their size along the
diagonal): an engine's parts sat one inside another and each face had to
be dug out to be picked (engine field test 0.7.4). A part goes to the
right of the parts already in the assembly, with a gap.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestAssemblySolve

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/Assembly/CommandInsertLink.py |  7 +++++++
 src/Mod/Assembly/UtilsAssembly.py     | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/Mod/Unified/TestAssemblySolve.py  | 20 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Mod/Assembly/CommandInsertLink.py b/src/Mod/Assembly/CommandInsertLink.py
index 6b043f9a8..de239511b 100644
--- a/src/Mod/Assembly/CommandInsertLink.py
+++ b/src/Mod/Assembly/CommandInsertLink.py
@@ -483,6 +483,13 @@ class TaskAssemblyInsertLink(QtCore.QObject):
 
         self.prevScreenCenter = screenCenter
 
+        # Beside the parts already there (to the right, with a gap), not on top of them: all the
